the greatness of Hinduism--its vitality, its earthiness, its vividness--lies precisely in many of those idiosyncratic qualities that continue to inspire debate today. Wendy Doniger, one of the world's foremost scholars of Hinduism, illuminates those moments within the tradition that resist forces that would standardize or establish a canon.--From publisher description."},"latest_revision":5,"revision":5,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2020-09-07T18:03:43.809535"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-10-09T01:59:13.573264"}}},"ISBN:9780199593347":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780199593347","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27690909M/The_Hindus","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL27690909M/The_Hindus","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9129740-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Oxford University Press, USA"],"number_of_pages":779,"subtitle":"An Alternative History","covers":[9129740],"physical_format":"paperback","full_title":"The Hindus An Alternative History","key":"/books/OL27690909M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7755241A","name":"Mircea Eliade"},{"key":"/authors/OL32073A","name":"Wendy Doniger"}],"source_records":["amazon:0199593345","bwb:9780199593347","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-022.mrc:82479496:802"],"title":"The Hindus","notes":"Source title: The Hindus: An Alternative History","identifiers":{"amazon":["0199593345"]},"publish_date":"Sep 01, 2010","works":[{"key":"/works/OL15178611W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"isbn_10":["0199593345"],"isbn_13":["9780199593347"],"classifications":{},"lc_classifications":["BL1150","BL1151.3"],"oclc_numbers":["615842469"],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2019-11-14T18:10:46.908177"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-06-18T10:35:22.948145"}}},"ISBN:9780143415343":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780143415343","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL62121175M/The_Hindus","preview":"r